From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 15:36:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: about 'what this is' + hide unimplemented proxy UI

web-app: link Imprint page from the About dialog

web-app: buttonify About dialog links with settings-style buttons

Replace the plain text links and footer actions in the About dialog with
SettingsIconButton rows, matching the Settings view. The links group
(SlothfulChat on GitHub, Delta Chat website) carries an open_in_new
indicator to signal they leave the app; Changelog and Imprint (both
local pages served alongside the app) and Help/View Log do not. Adds
buttons for the SlothfulChat GitHub repo and the changelog viewer we
ship at /changelog/, replacing the old link to GitHub releases.

Rebased onto v2.62.0: the onboarding screen's context menu now also
carries upstream's (experimental) Team Profile toggle (7ee712dbd), so
the menu stays and only its "Use Proxy" item is removed.
runtime.openLink() only takes http:/https: template strings since
56f5a6877, so the Changelog/Imprint URLs built from document.baseURI are
narrowed via a small localPage() helper.

Also hides upstream's "Hide menu bar" switch in Settings > Appearance,
which only ever showed disabled in a browser. And as proxies don't work
on wasm, a proxy QR code or link (scanned, pasted, opened, or the
chat-list search result upstream offers for a pasted one since #6752)
gets an alert saying so instead of the confirmation and the
ProxyConfiguration dialog. The check sits in useProcessQr before the
logged-in check, so every path gets the same answer, on the welcome
screen too. The string is a fork string.
